Frequently Asked Questions
What is AI-powered EHS software in mining?

AI-powered EHS software combines digital safety management workflows with artificial intelligence and analytics to help mining organizations manage hazards, incidents, inspections, risk assessments and preventive actions.

How can AI improve mining safety?

AI can help identify recurring risk patterns, analyze incident data, support visual hazard detection and prioritize corrective actions. Its recommendations require appropriate validation and human oversight.

Can AI predict mining accidents?

AI models may estimate elevated risk based on available data, but they cannot reliably predict every accident or guarantee prevention.

What are the benefits of digital EHS software for mining companies?

Potential benefits include more consistent inspections, improved action tracking, better visibility across sites, faster access to safety information and stronger documentation of risk controls.

Can digital EHS systems support underground mines?

Yes. Underground mining can benefit from digital inspections, incident management, risk assessments and connected monitoring, provided the solution is suitable for the site's connectivity, equipment and operational requirements.

Does AI replace mining safety officers?

No. AI is best used to assist qualified safety professionals. Responsibility for risk assessments, critical controls and safety decisions remains with authorized personnel.

